WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.200
It’s Monday, 9:07 AM. What blew up overnight?

00:03.200 --> 00:10.000
Forty-seven unread messages. Four conversations. Most notifications are not news.

00:10.000 --> 00:17.800
The database fell over. Kai picked it up. The runbook lied. The agent returns the owner, resolution, and open risk.

00:17.800 --> 00:25.000
Five months, three people, one printer. Search recovers the admin PIN from an ignored facilities message.

00:25.000 --> 00:31.000
Replies, reactions, and read-state changes stay behind explicit approval gates. Send nothing weird.

00:31.000 --> 00:37.000
Chrome LevelDB, cookie SQLite and WAL, Keychain decryption, token health, refresh, and isolated profiles keep the local path alive.

00:37.000 --> 00:42.000
Forty-seven unreads become one brief, then zero after approval. You ask once. It does the scrolling.
